From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Fri, 04 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] HACK: arm: kernel: sun5i AHB/MBUS settle after __create_page_tables

On Allwinner sun5i (R8/A13, C.H.I.P.) the kernel is completely silent
after the zImage decompressor jumps to the decompressed kernel.

Root cause: __create_page_tables writes 16 KB of page table data to
DRAM. The AHB/MBUS bus arbiter retains those write transactions. The
first DRAM read after returning to stext (literal pool load for
__mmap_switched address, or procinfo struct access) stalls the CPU
indefinitely.

Fix: at the end of __create_page_tables, before ret lr, issue a DSB +
busy-wait loop. The settle runs while still executing in the
__create_page_tables code region (a known-good instruction fetch path),
so the loop itself can execute. After the settle the bus is drained and
the return to stext proceeds cleanly.

  mcr p15, 0, r0, c7, c10, 4  @ ARMv5 DSB
  0x04000000 = 67,108,864 iters * ~3 cycles/iter @ 1 GHz ≈ 200 ms
  r0 is scratch at this point; r4/r8/r9/r10/lr are preserved.

Guarded by #ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
 arch/arm/kernel/head.S | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/kernel/head.S
+++ b/arch/arm/kernel/head.S
@@ -373,6 +373,22 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM_LPAE
 	sub	r4, r4, #0x1000		@ point to the PGD table
 #endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+	/*
+	 * sun5i AHB/MBUS bus stall: we just wrote 16 KB of page table
+	 * data to DRAM.  The AHB arbiter retains those write transactions;
+	 * the first DRAM read after returning to stext (literal pool /
+	 * procinfo) stalls the CPU indefinitely.
+	 * DSB + busy-wait drains the arbiter while still executing in the
+	 * __create_page_tables code region (known-good fetch path).
+	 * r0 is scratch here; r4/r8/r9/r10/lr are preserved.
+	 */
+	mcr	p15, 0, r0, c7, c10, 4		@ ARMv5 DSB
+	mov	r0, #0x04000000			@ 67M iters ≈ 200ms @ 1 GHz
+sun5i_pgtbl_settle:
+	subs	r0, r0, #1
+	bne	sun5i_pgtbl_settle
+#endif
 	ret	lr
 ENDPROC(__create_page_tables)
 	.ltorg
